Here are a few ways to write a TypeScript function to remove duplicates from an array, depending on whether you need to preserve the original order or not.

### 1. Using `Set` (Recommended for simplicity and order preservation)

The `Set` object in JavaScript/TypeScript only stores unique values. We can convert the array to a `Set` and then back to an array using the spread operator (`...`).

```typescript
/**
 * Removes duplicate elements from an array while preserving the original order of first appearance.
 *
 * @param arr The input array which may contain duplicates.
 * @returns A new array containing only the unique elements.
 */
function removeDuplicates<T>(arr: T[]): T[] {
  return [...new Set(arr)];
}

// Example Usage:
