```

### 2. Using `filter` and `indexOf` (Good for older environments or explicit iteration)

This method iterates through the array and keeps an element only if its first occurrence index matches the current index.

```typescript
/**
 * Removes duplicate elements from an array by checking the first index of each element.
 * Preserves the original order.
 *
 * @param arr The input array which may contain duplicates.
 * @returns A new array containing only the unique elements.
 */
function removeDuplicatesByFilter<T>(arr: T[]): T[] {
  return arr.filter((item: T, index: number): boolean => {
    // Keep the item only if its first occurrence is at the current index
    return arr.indexOf(item) === index;
  });
}

