1.  **`bubbleSort(int arr[], int n)` Function:**
    *   It takes an integer array (`arr`) and its size (`n`) as input.
    *   **Outer Loop (`for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++)`):** This loop controls the number of passes required. After each pass, the largest unsorted element "bubbles up" to its correct final position at the end of the unsorted portion. We need at most $n-1$ passes.
